.TH GIT-MIRROR-GHTEST.SH 1 "2026-04-25" "GitMirror" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
git-mirror-ghtest.sh \- dry-run GitHub repository discovery for mirror input validation
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B bash git-mirror-ghtest.sh
.RI [ github-user ... ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B git-mirror-ghtest.sh
queries public repositories from the GitHub API and prints repositories that would be considered for mirroring.
.PP
Behavior summary:
.IP "-"
Uses command-line users when provided.
.IP "-"
If no users are provided, reads
.B GH_USERS
from
.B config.json
.
.IP "-"
Skips forked repositories.
.IP "-"
Skips repositories listed in
.B GH_EXCLUDE_REPOS
from
.B config.json
.
.IP "-"
Prints matching repositories with a check mark and excluded repositories with an exclusion marker.
.PP
This script does not create, clone, or sync repositories in Gitea.
.SH OPTIONS
No flags are supported.
.PP
Positional arguments:
.TP
.I github-user
One or more GitHub usernames or organizations to inspect.
.SH FILES
.TP
.B config.json
Optional source of
.B GH_USERS
and
.B GH_EXCLUDE_REPOS
.
.SH EXIT STATUS
Returns 0 on normal completion. Returns 2 for invalid usage or missing prerequisites.
.SH EXAMPLES
Use configured users from config.json:
.PP
.B bash git-mirror-ghtest.sh
.PP
Check specific users:
.PP
.B bash git-mirror-ghtest.sh octocat github
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR git-mirror.sh (1),
.BR curl (1),
.BR jq (1)
